# === Compiled binary ===
# Anchored: `go build -o goscape-singleplayer` writes it to the repo root.
/goscape-singleplayer
*.exe

# === Runtime state ===
# The world database (goscape.db*), player saves and the ondemand public dir
# all live under --data-dir, which defaults to ./data. None of it is source.
/data/
# Generated by `make embed-pack`: the packed game cache embedded into release
# binaries. Never committed — it is 39 MB of build output, and every `go get`
# of this module would otherwise pay for it.
/internal/content/embedded/bundle/
# Written by `make embed-pack`/`embed-pack-fixture` only after the bundle
# above finishes successfully; `build-embedded` refuses to run without it, so
# a partial bundle from a failed pack is never silently embedded.
/internal/content/embedded/.bundle-complete

# === Test / coverage / profiling output ===
*.test
coverage.txt
coverage.html
*.prof
*.pprof
*.pb.gz
# SIGUSR1 pprof captures written by the client's pkg/profiling.
/profiles/

# === Local / private config — never push ===
# Claude Code: per-user local settings + personal session state. To SHARE
# team config, un-ignore specific paths, e.g.:
#   !.claude/settings.json
.claude/
# Project MCP config can carry server URLs / tokens — ignore by default.
.mcp.json
# Private per its own header (CLAUDE.md, by contrast, stays committed).
CLAUDE.local.md

# === Editors / IDEs ===
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# === Tool caches ===
.serena/
# superpowers SDD scratch workspace (ledger, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# === OS cruft ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
